  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1221 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nWarm and dry conditions will continue today and tomorrow before our \nnext cold front moves across the region Tuesday afternoon to the \novernight hours. Cooler temperatures and drier weather are \nexpected in the wake of the front with PWAT values peaking around \n0.80\". Now with the front that will be a different story. There's \na medium to high chance for showers and thunderstorms across the \nCoastal Bend, Coastal Plains and Victoria Crossroads with the best\nchances being in the Victoria Crossroads. The Brush Country will \nhave low chances of precipitation with the front. The environment \nwill be capable of producing strong thunderstorms with gusty \nwinds. \n\nMoisture is expected to advect back into the area late Thursday into \nThursday night with onshore flow which will increase our rain \nchances during the overnight hours and into Friday. Models are also \nbeginning to show a more significant cool down with another \ndisturbance next weekend, which could bring back increased rain \nchances and lows in the 50s.",
